lesson:
```
static double Area(double length, double width)
{
    return length * width;
}
static double Acres(double m2) => m2 / 4046.86;      // expression-bodied: one line
static double Total(int qty, double price, double discountPercent = 0)
{
    return Math.Round(qty * price * (100 - discountPercent) / 100, 2);
}
```

- `void` means no return value.
- Optional parameters have defaults: `Total(3, 50)` and `Total(4, 25.5, 10)` both work. You can also name arguments: `Total(qty: 3, price: 50)`.
- `out` parameters return extra values: `int.TryParse(text, out int n)`.
- Methods named in PascalCase. One job each; return instead of printing.

In Unity, your scripts are classes and their methods (`Start`, `Update`, `OnTriggerEnter`) are called by the engine at the right moments: the same idea, someone else calls your methods.

example.code:
using System;

class Program
{
    static void Main()
    {
        Console.WriteLine(Area(40, 30));
        Console.WriteLine(Total(4, 25.5, 10));
        Console.WriteLine(Total(3, 50));
    }

    static double Area(double w, double h) => w * h;

    static double Total(int qty, double price, double discount = 0)
    {
        return Math.Round(qty * price * (100 - discount) / 100, 2);
    }
}

